                <pb facs="0143" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4885/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Monroe to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                            Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-08-05"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 5, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 389.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that during
                    Friday night, July 24, 1908, Dr. Fernando E. Guachalla, President-elect of
                    Bolivia, died. The Government flags were at half-staff for three days, as was
                    the flag of this legation. Dr. Claudio Pinilla, minister for foreign affairs of
                    Bolivia, asks me to thank my Government for the sympathy expressed in its name
                    on the occasion of the death of Dr. Guachalla.</p>
                <p>I have, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L. Monroe,</hi> Jr.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
